WEBVTT

00:06.548 --> 00:09.092
[theme music]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.088
[siren blaring]

00:48.673 --> 00:50.216
EMERGENCY

00:51.468 --> 00:53.136
[wind gusting]

01:00.185 --> 01:02.645
[phone ringing]

01:04.397 --> 01:06.024
Hello. This is Team Two.

01:06.858 --> 01:08.109
Yes. Why?

01:09.652 --> 01:11.654
What? An accident?

01:12.238 --> 01:14.282
[tense music]

01:16.493 --> 01:18.745
"Accident"? What accident?

01:20.205 --> 01:22.123
- [Dong-han] Did someone get hurt?
- [Soo-jin gasps]

01:26.711 --> 01:29.297
[siren blaring]

01:29.380 --> 01:30.673
[paramedic] Turn it around.

01:34.511 --> 01:35.637
Hurry, hurry.

01:36.513 --> 01:38.264
Doctor! Doctor!

01:38.348 --> 01:40.058
- [nurse] It's critical.
- [moans in pain]

01:41.309 --> 01:42.727
Healthy, late 20s, male.

01:42.811 --> 01:46.147
[paramedic] Injured in an explosive blast,
unable to open his eyes.

01:46.231 --> 01:48.149
100 over 60, 120bpm.

01:48.233 --> 01:49.859
- Treatment room. Go now.
- Yes, sir.

01:52.028 --> 01:54.114
- Does this patient have a guardian?
- [Yu-jin] I'm here.

01:54.197 --> 01:55.323
I'm here for him.

01:55.824 --> 01:57.534
Can I get his family and first name?

01:57.617 --> 02:01.079
- [paper rustles]
- Lee Si-woo. He's with the KMA.

02:02.997 --> 02:04.249
[worried mumbling]

02:05.083 --> 02:06.459
[Dong-han] Who's hurt?

02:07.502 --> 02:08.670
It's Mr. Lee.

02:08.753 --> 02:10.547
[tense music]

02:14.509 --> 02:16.302
The hospital says he's very hurt.

02:25.103 --> 02:26.855
[Ha-kyung] You should go, Forecaster Lee.

02:28.606 --> 02:29.983
[Si-woo sighs]

02:31.526 --> 02:32.569
I have to go where?

02:32.652 --> 02:34.320
The Jeju Typhoon Center.

02:34.404 --> 02:35.446
You're a good fit.

02:39.868 --> 02:41.035
Are you kidding me?

02:41.744 --> 02:44.205
All the decisions I make at work
are taken seriously.

02:46.624 --> 02:50.253
So that means
you've given this considerable thought.

02:52.046 --> 02:54.591
Mm-hmm. If you're okay with it.

02:58.052 --> 03:00.513
[Si-woo] If the body temperature drops
about one degree,

03:00.597 --> 03:03.850
its level of immunity
becomes 30 percent weaker.

03:05.935 --> 03:08.897
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody
unless there's a chance of marriage.

03:10.189 --> 03:11.816
You are aware of that, right?

03:12.317 --> 03:17.196
[Si-woo] That means it becomes that much
more vulnerable to external threats.

03:19.991 --> 03:21.075
What are you…

03:21.951 --> 03:23.244
What's this about?

03:23.328 --> 03:25.079
We both need space.

03:25.747 --> 03:27.749
I think it's important for both of us.

03:28.791 --> 03:29.918
Yu-jin.

03:30.001 --> 03:34.047
We should take some time to think
how we can make this work.

03:34.756 --> 03:35.924
[sighs]

03:36.007 --> 03:38.343
You know you need it as much as I do.

03:46.059 --> 03:50.188
We do have some time still,
so you can let me know.

03:51.564 --> 03:53.733
[inhales]
Uh, no.

03:54.943 --> 03:55.985
I'll do it.

03:56.653 --> 03:58.071
You should give it more thought.

03:58.154 --> 04:02.075
There's nothing to go over now.
Like you said, it's official business.

04:02.158 --> 04:03.952
[inhales]
I'll go.

04:04.035 --> 04:07.622
[gentle music]

04:09.457 --> 04:10.667
It's settled.

04:14.796 --> 04:16.839
Anything you want to say?

04:16.923 --> 04:18.258
Oh, no.

04:22.845 --> 04:24.097
Okay.

04:32.772 --> 04:35.608
[Si-woo] The same goes
for the temperature between two people.

04:40.822 --> 04:44.117
If you leave me right now,
then that's it for us.

04:46.202 --> 04:47.620
Have you thought carefully about this?

04:50.665 --> 04:52.125
[sighs]

04:52.208 --> 04:53.626
If that's what you want…

04:54.919 --> 04:56.129
well, okay.

05:05.305 --> 05:06.389
[door closes]

05:08.891 --> 05:11.519
[luggage rattling]

05:15.857 --> 05:18.943
[woman on PA system]
The 77-4 bus will be arriving shortly.

05:31.414 --> 05:33.958
[brakes squeal]

05:34.042 --> 05:35.251
[bus door opens]

05:41.466 --> 05:43.051
[bus door squeaking]

05:48.973 --> 05:51.309
[Si-woo] One tiny thing
someone says to you,

05:51.392 --> 05:57.315
one small twitch of their face
can sometimes turn your emotions ice-cold.

05:59.817 --> 06:00.943
And…

06:03.988 --> 06:05.156
[Soo-jin] Oh, no.

06:07.283 --> 06:09.702
There was an accident?
Where? Where and how bad was it?

06:10.328 --> 06:12.914
Ho… hold on a moment. Who is this?

06:12.997 --> 06:14.791
If you tell me
which hospital it is, I'll--

06:14.874 --> 06:17.627
- [Yu-jin] This is Chae Yu-jin.
- [gasps]

06:22.173 --> 06:23.049
[moans]

06:25.134 --> 06:27.261
I'm with Si-woo right now.

06:28.262 --> 06:32.475
[Si-woo] When your emotional temperature
drops even one degree,

06:33.101 --> 06:39.273
you become highly sensitive,
vulnerable to the outside environment.

06:49.450 --> 06:50.284
[beeps]

06:53.121 --> 06:57.542
EPISODE 11
1

06:58.376 --> 07:00.169
2 DAYS AGO

07:00.253 --> 07:03.589
[bright music]

07:12.348 --> 07:14.725
[upbeat music]

07:33.536 --> 07:34.829
[squeaks]

07:49.760 --> 07:52.597
[reporter on TV] Watch out for signs
of physical and mental exhaustion

07:52.680 --> 07:54.182
as the hot weather continues.

07:54.265 --> 07:57.643
Heat wave advisories have been issued
in the Yeongnam area

07:57.727 --> 07:59.520
- and most of the western region.
- [sighs]

07:59.604 --> 08:02.440
And the heat wave warning
has been issued in Gwangju.

08:05.776 --> 08:07.153
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

08:07.904 --> 08:10.531
Ah, hell. No sign of rain yet, Director?

08:10.615 --> 08:14.535
There will be a light rain under 5mm
from the wind on the east coast.

08:14.619 --> 08:16.662
However, it will only reach Gangwon.

08:17.246 --> 08:20.249
That doesn't even count as rain, really.
[sighs]

08:20.917 --> 08:22.376
Wow, red across the board.

08:22.460 --> 08:24.962
The Ministry of the Interior and Safety
is going on the news

08:25.046 --> 08:26.631
to announce some safety measures today.

08:26.714 --> 08:30.301
Local governments have agreed
to try and set up heat shelter facilities.

08:30.384 --> 08:32.553
- Okay.
- [Dong-han sighs]

08:32.637 --> 08:35.014
A lot of government offices
are gonna get hit hard, huh?

08:35.097 --> 08:36.349
- [Bong-chan] It's inevitable.
- [phone vibrates]

08:36.432 --> 08:38.142
[Si-woo] What shall we do this weekend?

08:38.226 --> 08:39.894
It's the last one before I leave for Jeju.

08:40.478 --> 08:41.979
What are you doing?

08:42.563 --> 08:43.773
[whispers]
What's wrong?

08:45.816 --> 08:46.859
What? Go ahead.

08:47.527 --> 08:48.569
Uh, yes, sir.

08:48.653 --> 08:51.197
Let's start with impact forecast
for each region affected.

08:51.280 --> 08:52.573
[phone vibrates]

08:52.657 --> 08:54.659
[Si-woo] How about
duck baeksuk in Gapyeong?

08:55.243 --> 08:57.119
Duck baeksuk in Gapyeong--

08:57.203 --> 08:58.162
Hmm?

08:58.246 --> 09:01.415
[comical music]

09:05.503 --> 09:06.963
I apologize.

09:07.046 --> 09:10.049
Uh, I think that an emphasis
on water temperature control

09:10.132 --> 09:12.677
and shading near fish farms
would be appropriate.

09:13.761 --> 09:17.765
Oh, and let's remind the press
to restrain from their catastrophizing.

09:17.848 --> 09:19.225
We'll do our best, Director.

09:19.308 --> 09:20.309
Thanks.

09:20.810 --> 09:23.062
If there's nothing further,
we'll adjourn this meeting.

09:23.145 --> 09:24.981
- Good work, all.
- Great work.

09:25.064 --> 09:26.357
- Great job.
- [all] Thank you.

09:26.440 --> 09:29.068
[man] Duck baeksuk in Gapyeong
sounds pretty good.

09:29.151 --> 09:32.113
[Bong-chan] Oh, right.
Did you make your decision?

09:33.489 --> 09:36.117
- The typhoon center, who's going?
- Uh, yes.

09:36.659 --> 09:39.537
- It's typhoon season already?
- Yeah, someone's gotta go.

09:39.620 --> 09:41.205
Well, who is it, huh?

09:41.289 --> 09:43.457
You don't think it could be me, do you?

09:43.541 --> 09:44.584
[Myung-ju sighs]

09:47.211 --> 09:48.421
What? You haven't decided yet?

09:51.257 --> 09:52.592
I'm going, sir. It's me.

09:54.510 --> 09:56.887
Huh? It's you? Since when?

09:56.971 --> 09:58.973
Yesterday.
[chuckles]

09:59.056 --> 10:00.349
- Oh!
- Congratulations.

10:00.433 --> 10:02.393
- [Soo-jin] Congrats.
- [Bong-chan] Okay, then.

10:02.476 --> 10:04.812
Forecaster Lee and Director Jin,
I'll see you in my office.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.063
Yes, sir.

10:07.148 --> 10:09.025
[phone vibrates]

10:10.985 --> 10:13.446
Oh, Bo-mi. Hey.

10:15.156 --> 10:16.657
[Dong-han] Oh, okay.

10:17.199 --> 10:19.118
I wish I could go to Jeju.

10:20.286 --> 10:21.829
[Ha-kyung] You seem
so excited to go to Jeju.

10:21.912 --> 10:24.874
[Si-woo] I'm not excited about Jeju.
I'm excited about the typhoon center.

10:24.957 --> 10:26.792
I've always wanted to work there.

10:26.876 --> 10:29.086
You know me. I love field work.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.380
You told me that Headquarters
was your dream.

10:31.464 --> 10:33.132
Now you're saying you prefer the field?

10:33.215 --> 10:35.426
What can I say? I'm multi-talented.

10:36.719 --> 10:39.388
Good for you and, uh, best of luck.

10:39.472 --> 10:42.391
What's wrong?
You're the one that told me to go.

10:44.143 --> 10:47.063
Anyway, I don't like
the duck baeksuk in Gapyeong idea.

10:51.651 --> 10:52.610
[sighs]

11:08.250 --> 11:10.753
[keyboards clacking]

11:14.382 --> 11:17.676
We will now begin the briefing
for the 29th of July.

11:18.260 --> 11:21.347
Currently in Korea, the lower atmosphere
is filled with hot and humid air,

11:21.430 --> 11:24.308
and the upper atmosphere
is filled with hot and dry air.

11:24.934 --> 11:26.102
The cause of this heat wave

11:26.185 --> 11:29.522
is the North Pacific anticyclone
which has expanded to the south

11:29.605 --> 11:33.234
and also the Tibetan anticyclone
from inland China heading westward.

11:42.701 --> 11:45.746
ELECTRONIC CIVIL SERVICE CENTER
DIVORCE

11:48.666 --> 11:50.251
[mouse clicks]

11:51.585 --> 11:53.671
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

11:53.754 --> 11:57.299
[pensive music]

12:09.895 --> 12:11.605
[chuckling]

12:22.032 --> 12:23.576
- Boo!
- [gasps]

12:23.659 --> 12:25.161
What are you doing?

12:25.244 --> 12:29.123
[laughs]
I thought I wouldn't see you here.

12:29.206 --> 12:31.000
I told you my school trip
has one more day here.

12:31.083 --> 12:32.334
So when's it done?

12:32.418 --> 12:35.045
The last part's the weather chart
listing in ten minutes.

12:35.129 --> 12:37.923
So we could have, uh, a bite soon, yeah?

12:38.007 --> 12:39.925
The food at the cafeteria here
is really good.

12:40.009 --> 12:41.010
Hmm…

12:42.178 --> 12:43.012
Well, okay.

12:43.721 --> 12:44.680
[chuckles]

12:45.806 --> 12:47.016
What time should I be there?

12:47.099 --> 12:49.101
Ah, you just call me, okay?

12:49.185 --> 12:50.561
After class, yeah?

12:50.644 --> 12:51.729
Okay.

12:53.397 --> 12:55.065
Tomorrow?

12:55.149 --> 12:56.317
[Bong-chan] Mm-hmm.

12:57.651 --> 12:59.612
- Why? Should he not?
- It's too soon, sir.

12:59.695 --> 13:01.280
I thought we'd have the whole week.

13:01.363 --> 13:04.617
[Bong-chan] You know Director Sung
at the typhoon center. She's impatient.

13:05.493 --> 13:06.869
All week, she's been bugging me

13:06.952 --> 13:09.538
about when we're gonna send her
our forecaster.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.248
She says they should come ASAP

13:11.332 --> 13:13.792
to get acquainted
with the station practices,

13:14.543 --> 13:16.504
to avoid any mistakes
when the typhoons really start.

13:16.587 --> 13:17.838
What could I say?

13:17.922 --> 13:20.633
I get her concerns.
But we have our own problems here.

13:20.716 --> 13:23.511
You know it's crazy
because of the heat wave right now.

13:24.345 --> 13:28.057
Couldn't he continue covering
all of that from down there? Huh?

13:28.807 --> 13:30.434
- Uh…
- And aside from the heat,

13:30.518 --> 13:32.937
I only told him
he's going to Jeju yesterday.

13:33.521 --> 13:35.481
- [Ha-kyung] He needs time to prepare.
- No, it's fine.

13:37.441 --> 13:38.734
He says it's fine, see?

13:38.817 --> 13:41.946
Yeah. Of course, I can cover
the heat wave from Jeju.

13:42.029 --> 13:43.364
It's really not a problem.

13:43.447 --> 13:45.032
[Bong-chan] Okay! Great, then.

13:45.616 --> 13:47.701
If that's really all,
he'll go this weekend.

13:47.785 --> 13:50.120
All right. Dismissed.
[clears throat]

13:50.996 --> 13:52.331
[Bong-chan sighs]
Jeez.

13:53.499 --> 13:54.583
[door opens]

14:02.967 --> 14:05.219
- [door closes]
- You can't just say yes so impulsively.

14:05.302 --> 14:07.721
How are you gonna leave tomorrow?
You're not ready to go.

14:07.805 --> 14:10.182
You didn't even want to go to Gapyeong
for duck baeksuk.

14:10.266 --> 14:12.017
I don't have any weekend plans,

14:12.101 --> 14:14.645
so I might as well go
to the typhoon center and work.

14:15.396 --> 14:17.106
Are you serious or just making a scene?

14:17.189 --> 14:19.149
Mm, half and half.

14:20.526 --> 14:22.653
Regardless. We can talk to him again.

14:23.362 --> 14:24.738
[Si-woo] Why are you flip-flopping?

14:24.822 --> 14:26.907
This is also confusing now.

14:30.119 --> 14:31.120
What do you mean?

14:31.203 --> 14:34.373
Didn't you want some time for yourself,
away from me?

14:35.708 --> 14:38.294
Isn't that why you wanted me
to go to Jeju?

14:38.919 --> 14:42.172
Then how come you're mad
that I would leave a few days earlier?

14:43.507 --> 14:46.302
[pensive music]

14:46.385 --> 14:48.220
I think you're mistaken about something.

14:48.304 --> 14:52.057
I don't ever let my own feelings get
in the way of official weather business.

14:52.141 --> 14:55.352
Even in other relationships,
not once did I do that.

14:55.436 --> 14:58.314
[breathes deeply]

14:58.981 --> 15:01.817
There's no need for us
to talk to the General Director.

15:01.901 --> 15:05.446
I'll just head out tomorrow, Director.

15:14.163 --> 15:16.165
[pensive music]

15:26.926 --> 15:28.636
- Reporter Cho.
- Yes?

15:28.719 --> 15:31.013
Is Reporter Chae not here
for the briefing?

15:31.764 --> 15:35.059
Uh… Oh, uh, I heard she took time off.

15:35.142 --> 15:36.518
You haven't heard?

15:36.602 --> 15:39.730
[gasps]
Ah! So that was today.

15:40.439 --> 15:41.482
Yes.

15:41.565 --> 15:44.777
- [both chuckling]
- I, uh, forgot when she was… Yeah.

15:44.860 --> 15:46.820
- Right. Goodbye. See you.
- Okay, see you.

15:54.495 --> 15:56.497
[gentle music]

16:03.420 --> 16:06.298
WEATHER

16:09.718 --> 16:11.887
[phone vibrates]

16:15.724 --> 16:17.977
KI-JUN

16:21.605 --> 16:22.648
[phone clacks]

16:25.818 --> 16:27.111
[phone vibrates]

16:28.654 --> 16:29.488
[Ki-jun] You took time off?

16:32.157 --> 16:34.493
Seriously? Where are you right now?

16:35.202 --> 16:37.746
Come back home. We need to talk in person.

16:38.914 --> 16:41.000
[deep sigh]

16:46.296 --> 16:49.758
FLIGHT RESERVATION

16:52.219 --> 16:54.430
FROM SEOUL TO JEJU ISLAND

16:54.513 --> 16:56.890
BOOK A FLIGHT

17:00.561 --> 17:03.439
[breathes deeply]

17:09.820 --> 17:12.114
[breathes deeply]

17:13.323 --> 17:14.450
[Ki-jun] Yu-jin.

17:28.005 --> 17:29.798
[sighs]

17:44.605 --> 17:45.981
[phone vibrates]

17:47.775 --> 17:50.110
[Myung-ju] What's up?
The vibe is off here.

17:52.780 --> 17:55.949
[Soo-jin] I think something went down
between the Director and Forecaster Lee

17:56.033 --> 17:57.576
about the typhoon center.

17:57.659 --> 17:59.203
You should do something, Mrs. Oh.

17:59.286 --> 18:01.371
- I should?
- Huh?

18:01.455 --> 18:04.416
[quirky music]

18:04.500 --> 18:06.710
You have something to say, Ms. Oh?

18:06.794 --> 18:07.711
Uh, do I?

18:09.755 --> 18:12.299
Uh, it's…
[light chuckle]

18:13.383 --> 18:14.718
[Myung-ju] Director…

18:15.636 --> 18:17.721
So should we go for dinner later?

18:17.805 --> 18:19.556
[playful music]

18:21.809 --> 18:23.018
Wait, dinner?

18:23.727 --> 18:25.270
Uh, well…
[chuckles]

18:25.354 --> 18:27.022
Forecaster Lee is going to Jeju,

18:27.106 --> 18:31.527
and of course he'll come back soon
since it's just a temporary dispatch.

18:32.111 --> 18:33.237
But still, it would be nice

18:33.320 --> 18:35.572
to have dinner together
and wish him luck before he leaves.

18:36.156 --> 18:37.241
What do you say?

18:37.324 --> 18:38.200
Sounds great.

18:38.784 --> 18:39.827
Oh.
[chuckles]

18:39.910 --> 18:42.788
Yeah, sure. Sounds great.
[awkward chuckle]

18:42.871 --> 18:44.915
Mr. Shin, what do you say?

18:44.998 --> 18:47.000
- I already have plans.
- [Myung-ju] Ah.

18:47.584 --> 18:49.002
Could you reschedule?

18:49.628 --> 18:51.922
It's the first Team Two dinner altogether.

18:52.464 --> 18:54.675
Oh, that's true, though.
It'd be the first time.

18:54.758 --> 18:57.052
[Soo-jin] We've never done that before
with this crew.

18:57.136 --> 19:00.681
Well, it'd be great if you rescheduled,
Mr. Shin, to be with our team.

19:00.764 --> 19:02.182
I really shouldn't. It's important.

19:02.808 --> 19:04.059
[Seok-ho] I'm sorry.

19:04.643 --> 19:07.813
Oh, well, I suppose it is what it is.

19:08.438 --> 19:09.898
Let's do it.

19:09.982 --> 19:11.233
Huh?

19:11.900 --> 19:14.278
We should have a dinner
whoever can make it.

19:15.028 --> 19:16.363
What do you say, Forecaster?

19:18.740 --> 19:19.658
Yeah.

19:21.910 --> 19:24.496
Well, okay, then.
I'll, uh, get us a reservation.

19:25.581 --> 19:26.874
[chuckles anxiously]

19:38.343 --> 19:40.470
[sighs]

19:45.100 --> 19:46.560
[door opens]

19:49.146 --> 19:50.564
[door closes]

19:54.943 --> 19:57.988
What's wrong?
This entire dinner thing is just for you.

20:03.076 --> 20:04.953
Why are you upset right now?

20:06.538 --> 20:07.706
"Right now"?

20:08.790 --> 20:11.418
I've never said I'm upset before,
so why would you say "right now"?

20:13.045 --> 20:15.589
I've never once told you I'm upset

20:15.672 --> 20:17.799
since the moment you said
I should go to Jeju.

20:18.550 --> 20:21.136
- What's wrong with you, kid?
- [Si-woo] I'm not a kid.

20:21.220 --> 20:22.554
I'm a man.

20:22.638 --> 20:24.097
And in fact, I'm yours.

20:25.974 --> 20:28.894
[water boiling]

20:31.188 --> 20:32.189
[clicks]

20:39.363 --> 20:41.156
[indistinct chatter]

20:41.240 --> 20:42.991
Hey. Enjoy your lunch.

20:43.075 --> 20:45.035
- Oh, hello.
- Hey.

20:45.118 --> 20:46.745
- Who is this?
- My daughter.

20:46.828 --> 20:49.248
- Oh, your daughter? Go ahead. Here.
- Please go ahead. Go.

20:49.331 --> 20:51.583
- Sure, thanks.
- Adorable.

20:52.584 --> 20:54.461
She's here for her school.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.213
[server] Oh, she's so pretty.

20:56.296 --> 20:58.048
- Right? Yup, she is.
- Uh-huh.

20:58.131 --> 20:59.508
[chuckling]

20:59.591 --> 21:04.137
Ah! Here at the, uh, KMA,
the forecasters have the most work,

21:04.221 --> 21:07.432
so, uh, the… the others all know that,

21:07.516 --> 21:10.519
so most of the time,
they'll let us eat first at lunch.

21:11.603 --> 21:13.480
- Thank you. Oh, that's great.
- [server] Here.

21:17.484 --> 21:18.819
Have some vegetables.

21:22.447 --> 21:24.241
Oh, they got sausage.

21:25.075 --> 21:27.828
[Dong-han] When I was a kid,
I had this all the time.

21:28.537 --> 21:30.414
It's really good.
[chuckles]

21:30.497 --> 21:33.917
[light upbeat music]

21:34.001 --> 21:36.753
Mm, yeah. Mm.

21:36.837 --> 21:38.630
Can we join you for lunch?

21:38.714 --> 21:40.549
- Yeah, sure. Here.
- Oh, of course.

21:40.632 --> 21:42.884
- [Soo-jin] Slide in right here.
- Oh, thanks.

21:43.510 --> 21:45.345
This is my daughter, Um Bo-mi.

21:45.429 --> 21:46.805
Ah, Um Bo-mi, huh?

21:46.888 --> 21:49.182
- [Soo-jin] Hello.
- [Myung-ju] Hello.

21:49.266 --> 21:52.144
These are some of the people
who work with me on the team.

21:53.061 --> 21:54.146
Hello.

21:54.229 --> 21:55.397
- Aw.
- Hello.

21:55.480 --> 21:57.524
- She's beautiful.
- Right?

21:57.607 --> 21:59.151
I guess she takes after her mom.

21:59.234 --> 22:00.527
What are you saying?

22:00.610 --> 22:03.697
Hey, I can see some
of her Papa's features there too.

22:03.780 --> 22:06.241
Can you tell me
what brings you here, Bo-mi?

22:06.325 --> 22:08.493
- Your Papa, huh?
- No, she's here for her school.

22:08.577 --> 22:11.830
- [Soo-jin] Oh, a field trip.
- Mm. So, uh, do you like science?

22:11.913 --> 22:13.498
Yes, I do.

22:13.582 --> 22:14.916
- [Myung-ju chuckles]
- How did you know?

22:15.834 --> 22:17.461
I heard students who come to our office

22:17.544 --> 22:21.214
are looking for experience in fields
they like for their school records.

22:21.298 --> 22:22.341
- I see.
- [Soo-jin] Oh.

22:22.424 --> 22:24.384
[Myung-ju] You not only resemble your dad,

22:24.468 --> 22:26.470
I'd say you've got
a science mind too, huh?

22:26.553 --> 22:28.597
- Oh?
- You don't know?

22:28.680 --> 22:30.891
Your Pa's the best meteorologist in Korea.

22:30.974 --> 22:32.684
Oh, come on. That's not true.

22:32.768 --> 22:35.479
- [all laughing]
- [Myung-ju] You are the best.

22:36.855 --> 22:38.774
Bo-mi, here, try. Try this.

22:39.399 --> 22:42.110
[Soo-jin] Aw, look at Mr. Um.

22:42.194 --> 22:43.695
I didn't know you had a soft side.

22:43.779 --> 22:45.906
You're a real tiger in the situation room.

22:45.989 --> 22:48.116
- [Myung-ju chuckles]
- You're a lucky girl.

22:50.869 --> 22:51.953
Mr. Um, sir.

22:52.037 --> 22:53.997
Could I have a piece
of your sausage as well?

22:54.081 --> 22:55.332
- What's this?
- [Soo-jin] Hmm?

22:55.415 --> 22:56.708
[chuckles]
Can I?

22:57.375 --> 22:59.336
You can perfectly well
get your own sausage.

22:59.419 --> 23:00.337
Yup.

23:00.420 --> 23:02.297
- [chuckling]
- Bo-mi, try.

23:03.882 --> 23:04.925
Go on.

23:13.600 --> 23:15.310
[uneasy music]

23:15.393 --> 23:17.395
- It's good, right?
- [Myung-ju] You like it?

23:17.479 --> 23:19.356
[shy chuckle]

23:20.357 --> 23:22.651
[phone vibrates]

23:22.734 --> 23:23.985
Mm.

23:25.195 --> 23:26.363
Just a moment. Sorry.

23:26.446 --> 23:27.781
- Okay.
- [Dong-han] Mm-hmm.

23:29.950 --> 23:30.826
Eommoni.

23:30.909 --> 23:33.286
[Myung-ju's mom-in-law] You need
to pick up the kids a little early today.

23:33.370 --> 23:34.204
Huh?

23:34.287 --> 23:35.956
Maybe it's because of the hot weather.

23:36.039 --> 23:39.459
And my eyes hurt.
And I'm not feeling so great.

23:39.543 --> 23:42.003
Ah. Well, I'm sorry.

23:42.087 --> 23:45.799
We have a dinner with our, uh, department.

23:45.882 --> 23:48.260
[Myung-ju] One of the forecasters
is going to Jeju.

23:48.885 --> 23:51.680
The director herself arranged it,
so it'd be really hard for me

23:51.763 --> 23:52.681
to not be there.

23:52.764 --> 23:56.101
Uh, could my husband
just take the kids from you?

23:56.184 --> 23:58.103
He's studying now. You know that.

23:58.687 --> 23:59.771
[sighs]

24:01.648 --> 24:05.819
Then I'll be right over
as soon as I am all through eating.

24:06.653 --> 24:08.446
Okay. Yeah.

24:12.284 --> 24:14.494
[sighs]
What to do?

24:14.578 --> 24:17.414
I suggested it.
I can't back out of it now.

24:19.166 --> 24:20.417
[sighs]

24:22.252 --> 24:24.254
[pensive music]

24:27.048 --> 24:28.466
[Si-woo] I'm not a kid.

24:28.550 --> 24:30.260
I'm a man.

24:30.343 --> 24:31.887
And in fact, I'm yours.

24:34.181 --> 24:35.724
Hey, we're at work.

24:35.807 --> 24:37.726
Then maybe you should say "Forecaster."

24:39.352 --> 24:42.314
I know you want to…
to draw some kind of boundary

24:43.148 --> 24:45.233
between professional and personal with us.

24:45.317 --> 24:47.319
I understand how you feel,

24:47.402 --> 24:49.988
and I'll do what I can
to cooperate like I said.

24:50.071 --> 24:51.156
Still…

24:53.575 --> 24:54.784
I'm Si-woo.

24:56.328 --> 24:58.663
Not Han Ki-jun who you dated before.

24:59.247 --> 25:00.373
It's Si-woo.

25:03.335 --> 25:06.004
And none of this right now
is about that man.

25:06.087 --> 25:09.382
I know what you went through with him,
how hurt you were.

25:09.466 --> 25:11.551
I know why you're so scared
of office romance,

25:11.635 --> 25:14.095
and why you're worried
about everyone finding out, okay?

25:14.179 --> 25:17.140
Still, that was that relationship.

25:17.224 --> 25:19.100
And this one is ours now.

25:20.894 --> 25:23.271
I don't want you
comparing us all the time.

25:24.522 --> 25:25.482
It doesn't feel good.

25:25.565 --> 25:27.984
When did I ever compare you to Ki-jun?

25:30.070 --> 25:34.532
The reason that you
kept me a secret at a distance,

25:34.616 --> 25:38.161
treating me like a kid is all because
of what happened with Ki-jun, okay?

25:38.745 --> 25:42.415
You're afraid you might see him in me
and maybe get hurt in the same way.

25:42.999 --> 25:44.209
And get humiliated again…

25:45.418 --> 25:46.836
just like you did before.

25:47.629 --> 25:49.422
- Lee Si-woo…
- [Si-woo] It's true.

25:49.506 --> 25:51.132
I can't consider getting married.

25:51.216 --> 25:52.926
That's just not the way I'm built.

25:53.843 --> 25:57.097
But still, I still want
to be in love with you.

25:59.599 --> 26:00.976
I really…

26:03.311 --> 26:04.896
really adore you.

26:07.107 --> 26:08.149
And…

26:09.985 --> 26:12.237
if that's confusing at all, I'm sorry.

26:14.239 --> 26:16.116
I'm asking for just your love…

26:17.242 --> 26:20.996
when there's nothing in the world
that I could bring to this.

26:23.331 --> 26:24.541
And so…

26:25.834 --> 26:28.670
I would understand
if you want to reconsider us.

26:31.172 --> 26:32.132
You can.

26:34.050 --> 26:37.178
But I can't do this casual.

26:39.472 --> 26:43.393
I can't have some moderate tepid thing
where we draw lines for each other.

26:43.977 --> 26:45.478
I really don't think I could.

26:47.105 --> 26:48.898
What are you saying right now?

26:53.778 --> 26:54.988
That you can…

26:56.531 --> 26:58.700
While I'm in Jeju, think about it.

26:59.743 --> 27:01.703
If you want to continue…

27:04.456 --> 27:05.707
or break it off.

27:05.790 --> 27:10.170
["The Day You Were Falling"
by John Park playing]

27:15.884 --> 27:16.968
[door closes]

27:30.857 --> 27:32.525
[phone vibrates]

27:34.694 --> 27:36.946
FATHER

27:40.909 --> 27:43.328
- [phone vibrates]
- [sighs]

27:46.331 --> 27:48.208
[vibrating continues]

27:56.007 --> 27:57.801
[phone vibrates]

28:02.514 --> 28:04.307
Yes, Jin Ha-kyung.

28:07.185 --> 28:09.687
I'll look into that
and follow it up. Thank you.

28:09.771 --> 28:10.647
Okay.

28:13.274 --> 28:16.069
KMA HEAT WAVE FORECAST

28:16.152 --> 28:19.072
[eerie music]

28:19.155 --> 28:21.408
THE WORST HEAT WAVE EVER!
THERE'S NO END TO IT

28:21.491 --> 28:23.660
PEOPLE ARE GROWING TIRED
OF THE MURDEROUS HEAT

28:25.912 --> 28:26.955
[sighs]

28:28.498 --> 28:29.958
My god! This is ridiculous.

28:31.584 --> 28:34.587
[Soo-jin] A treat.
Thanks to lovely Bo-mi. Thank you.

28:34.671 --> 28:35.588
[chuckles]

28:36.297 --> 28:37.507
[can opening]

28:37.590 --> 28:39.426
Oh, Bo-mi's not here?

28:39.509 --> 28:40.760
- In the restroom.
- [Myung-ju] Oh.

28:40.844 --> 28:42.303
- Go ahead. Get a drink.
- On you?

28:42.387 --> 28:43.722
- Mm-hmm.
- I'll get that one, then.

28:43.805 --> 28:45.223
[coins clinking]

28:45.306 --> 28:46.933
- Is it good?
- [Soo-jin] Mm-hmm.

28:47.016 --> 28:48.768
[coughing]

28:56.693 --> 28:59.195
- [water running]
- [gasps, coughs]

29:00.739 --> 29:03.658
[ominous music]

29:07.454 --> 29:09.414
[coughs]

29:25.764 --> 29:27.307
[labored breathing]

29:28.266 --> 29:29.184
[coughs]

29:29.267 --> 29:31.478
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

29:31.561 --> 29:33.980
[gloomy music]

29:35.857 --> 29:37.817
[printer whirring]

29:44.324 --> 29:45.408
[sighs]

29:50.497 --> 29:53.166
[mouse clicking]

29:59.756 --> 30:02.133
[water running]

30:04.636 --> 30:06.930
- [choking]
- [door opens]

30:11.184 --> 30:12.435
- [thuds]
- Oh, gosh!

30:12.519 --> 30:14.687
Honey! Honey, are you okay?

30:14.771 --> 30:18.650
Appa. My father, please.

30:19.484 --> 30:20.652
Oh, my god.

30:20.735 --> 30:22.153
- [Soo-jin] She's lucky.
- It is luck.

30:22.237 --> 30:25.281
- Oh, I'm fair pretty too.
- [Soo-jin] If I just got her skin…

30:25.365 --> 30:26.574
[Si-woo] Did you have lunch?

30:26.658 --> 30:27.867
- Yeah.
- Oh, Forecaster.

30:27.951 --> 30:31.204
[woman] Hey! Someone, please help!
A student collapsed over here!

30:31.746 --> 30:33.456
A student's in there,
on the floor in the bathroom,

30:33.540 --> 30:34.833
- and she's choking.
- Um Bo-mi.

30:35.792 --> 30:37.460
- [gasps]
- [Myung-ju] Oh, my!

30:37.544 --> 30:40.171
- Hey! Call 119! 119! Hurry!
- Okay.

30:40.255 --> 30:42.257
[tense music]

30:43.633 --> 30:45.301
[siren wailing]

30:45.385 --> 30:48.429
EMERGENCY CENTER

30:49.097 --> 30:50.807
- [Dong-han] Hey.
- What's going on? Where is she?

30:50.890 --> 30:52.809
[sighs]
I don't know what…

30:53.393 --> 30:55.854
She was fine when we were having lunch,

30:55.937 --> 30:57.689
but she collapsed
in the bathroom right after.

30:57.772 --> 30:59.774
She couldn't breathe
and had a terrible sort of rash

30:59.858 --> 31:02.277
- on her whole neck that went down.
- And what did you feed her?

31:02.360 --> 31:03.820
She ate at the cafeteria.

31:03.903 --> 31:05.405
What was the food there, though?

31:07.282 --> 31:12.579
Uh, there was rice, seaweed,
and radish, pork sausage, and soup.

31:12.662 --> 31:14.122
You gave pork to our daughter?

31:14.706 --> 31:15.540
Yeah.

31:15.623 --> 31:18.042
Bo-mi has always been allergic to that.

31:18.710 --> 31:19.919
Did you forget?

31:21.546 --> 31:23.673
Bo-mi, here. Try this.

31:24.549 --> 31:27.552
[uneasy music]

31:32.307 --> 31:33.641
- It's good, right?
- [Myung-ju] You like it?

31:36.978 --> 31:38.855
I can't believe you.

31:43.401 --> 31:46.195
[gloomy music]

31:51.075 --> 31:52.118
[sighs]

31:56.706 --> 32:00.668
"The worst heat yet! No end in sight.
Murder by heat in Korea."

32:01.336 --> 32:03.963
I told you not to let them
get so sensational.

32:07.008 --> 32:08.426
Han Ki-jun, listen!

32:09.010 --> 32:10.511
Yu-jin has left.

32:11.095 --> 32:11.971
What?

32:12.055 --> 32:13.765
She wants to live alone.

32:15.725 --> 32:16.726
Why?

32:20.063 --> 32:21.898
What am I supposed to do now, Ha-kyung?

32:28.071 --> 32:29.447
[slurps]

32:36.746 --> 32:38.998
[somber music]

32:39.082 --> 32:41.709
[line dials, rings]

32:41.793 --> 32:42.794
[door closes]

32:44.253 --> 32:45.546
Hey, Mom.

32:46.172 --> 32:48.675
How are you? Everything good?

32:51.469 --> 32:54.138
No, I just miss you,
and I wanted to hear your voice.

32:57.600 --> 32:59.102
Yeah, he's doing well, of course.

33:01.771 --> 33:03.898
[Ki-jun] She doesn't pick up the phone.

33:03.982 --> 33:06.109
And she doesn't read my texts.

33:06.693 --> 33:08.277
How did this happen?

33:09.070 --> 33:11.906
Is it 'cause of her living with her ex?

33:14.117 --> 33:15.368
[sighs deeply]

33:15.994 --> 33:17.954
Uh, or did something else go down?

33:18.037 --> 33:19.163
Hey.

33:20.164 --> 33:22.792
Did you know that when we dated,

33:22.875 --> 33:27.088
I felt like your work was a whole lot
more important than me, you know?

33:28.923 --> 33:31.217
Every time I felt that way, I got sad

33:31.300 --> 33:33.886
because I felt like
I would always be your second.

33:34.971 --> 33:38.224
At the same time, I couldn't help
but feel like I was small and juvenile

33:38.307 --> 33:39.642
for having all of those thoughts.

33:42.854 --> 33:43.896
I did that to you?

33:44.647 --> 33:45.690
Mm-hmm.

33:46.691 --> 33:47.525
You did.

33:48.651 --> 33:51.863
You're very authoritative when you say
you need to focus on your work life.

33:53.781 --> 33:56.409
Of course, you said that to me
as a deputy director.

33:56.492 --> 33:58.327
Still, I was your boyfriend first.

33:59.537 --> 34:01.873
I felt awful so many times 'cause of that.

34:03.791 --> 34:09.172
I know you want to draw a boundary
between professional and personal with us.

34:09.255 --> 34:11.257
I understand how you feel,

34:11.340 --> 34:13.926
and I'll do what I can
to cooperate like I said.

34:14.010 --> 34:14.886
Still…

34:15.887 --> 34:17.180
But…
[Ki-jun sighs]

34:17.764 --> 34:18.598
[exhales sharply]

34:20.266 --> 34:23.853
One day, I realized that
I was doing the same thing to Yu-jin.

34:25.146 --> 34:28.357
I was comparing her to you
over every little thing.

34:29.317 --> 34:31.027
[Si-woo] That was that relationship.

34:31.110 --> 34:32.779
And this one is ours now.

34:33.362 --> 34:35.448
I don't want you comparing us
all the time.

34:36.949 --> 34:38.284
It doesn't feel good.

34:41.245 --> 34:44.207
Yu-jin is just Yu-jin.

34:45.625 --> 34:47.001
[Si-woo] I'm Si-woo.

34:47.085 --> 34:49.128
Not Han Ki-jun who you dated before.

34:49.212 --> 34:50.713
It's Si-woo.

34:50.797 --> 34:53.382
[Si-woo] And none of this right now
is about that man.

34:55.635 --> 34:56.469
[sighs]

34:56.552 --> 34:58.930
[pensive music]

34:59.013 --> 35:00.223
[sighs]

35:07.688 --> 35:09.649
[Myung-ju] Don't worry.
I took care of everything.

35:10.858 --> 35:12.985
Yeah. Ah, you're here.

35:13.069 --> 35:14.862
Mr. Um's daughter is okay.

35:15.446 --> 35:17.865
It looks like she made it through
the worst of it. She'll be all right.

35:18.658 --> 35:19.784
That's good.

35:20.660 --> 35:22.036
Uh, about our team dinner--

35:22.120 --> 35:24.872
Forecaster Lee is gonna meet us
straight at the restaurant.

35:24.956 --> 35:28.292
And Mr. Um will join us if the situation
with his daughter improves enough.

35:29.836 --> 35:30.795
[sighs]
Right.

35:30.878 --> 35:32.463
[relieved sigh]

35:36.259 --> 35:38.261
[pensive music]

35:47.311 --> 35:48.688
Here. Have this.

35:49.522 --> 35:50.648
Oh, thank you.

35:58.030 --> 36:00.491
Studying was the easiest thing
for me to do.

36:02.660 --> 36:05.872
I knew what I had to do
to get good grades.

36:05.955 --> 36:07.832
[breathes deeply]

36:07.915 --> 36:10.835
But this damn weather and family, though,

36:10.918 --> 36:13.212
I have no idea
how to wrap my head around it.

36:14.589 --> 36:17.466
There's no equation, manual.

36:18.968 --> 36:21.512
I never learned how to be a good father.

36:22.930 --> 36:25.683
I don't have the smallest idea…

36:26.309 --> 36:28.060
how to be a good husband or dad.

36:32.023 --> 36:34.025
The fact that you worry about all that…

36:34.734 --> 36:36.194
means you are one already.

36:38.988 --> 36:39.822
You know,

36:41.032 --> 36:45.411
I've never once seen my dad
think about any of that stuff.

36:50.082 --> 36:52.627
Just putting that out there.
[chuckles]

37:03.638 --> 37:04.680
How's Bo-mi?

37:06.224 --> 37:07.308
She's better now.

37:07.808 --> 37:10.394
[Hyang-rae] She'll have
to be discharged late tonight

37:11.312 --> 37:13.522
when the sedative they had
to give her has worn off.

37:14.357 --> 37:15.816
You should get going.

37:18.361 --> 37:20.613
I thought her dermatitis had improved.

37:22.240 --> 37:23.324
[Hyang-rae sighs]

37:24.659 --> 37:27.161
How many diseases in the world
just go away on their own?

37:28.329 --> 37:32.124
She stays well because of
the protection I provide her.

37:32.208 --> 37:34.543
What she eats, where she sleeps,
the clothes she wears.

37:37.046 --> 37:38.089
I'm sorry.

37:38.714 --> 37:39.590
For what?

37:39.674 --> 37:41.509
'Cause I almost killed her,

37:41.592 --> 37:44.345
pretending to be a good dad
and knowing nothing.

37:44.428 --> 37:45.554
[scoffs]

37:45.638 --> 37:46.889
How could you know…

37:49.225 --> 37:51.894
enough to be able to even pretend?

37:55.773 --> 37:57.441
[doors opens]

37:59.068 --> 38:00.403
[sighs]

38:02.780 --> 38:04.865
[phone vibrates]

38:12.373 --> 38:14.250
[crickets chirping]

38:15.793 --> 38:17.712
- Are you going out?
- Huh?

38:17.795 --> 38:20.506
Yeah. I have a research interview.

38:21.090 --> 38:22.300
Where are you going?

38:22.883 --> 38:24.385
Where do you have to go at night?

38:25.219 --> 38:26.971
You're not going to Ha-kyung's again.

38:27.054 --> 38:29.640
You think Ha-kyung's
the only thing important in my life?

38:30.349 --> 38:31.684
Well, sort of.

38:32.810 --> 38:33.811
Don't be late.

38:34.478 --> 38:36.063
And don't drink too much either.

38:39.191 --> 38:40.276
[huffs]

38:43.279 --> 38:45.656
MOTHER-IN-LAW

38:47.158 --> 38:49.535
[phone vibrates]

38:54.790 --> 38:57.209
- [Soo-jin] Are you sure you're okay?
- Hmm? Why?

38:57.793 --> 39:00.504
Your mother-in-law called.
She's been calling for a while now.

39:00.588 --> 39:01.589
[chuckles]

39:01.672 --> 39:05.217
If it's really so bad,
then she can call her own son.

39:05.843 --> 39:07.511
You know he's studying.

39:07.595 --> 39:11.432
Yes. And here I am
working to support him too.

39:11.515 --> 39:14.560
From time to time,
I need a little chance to breathe.

39:15.186 --> 39:16.937
I'm going to enjoy the food tonight.

39:17.021 --> 39:19.690
I'll eat and drink and noraebang later?

39:19.774 --> 39:21.025
[chuckles]

39:22.401 --> 39:25.196
Oh, uh, Mr. Shin. So what's he up to?

39:25.279 --> 39:27.323
Normally, he works and goes home.

39:27.907 --> 39:28.866
A new girlfriend?

39:29.825 --> 39:32.328
Ah, you know, he should
be dating at his age.

39:32.411 --> 39:33.746
Mm.

39:34.955 --> 39:37.416
- [Myung-ju] Director. Over here.
- Here.

39:38.250 --> 39:39.210
Oh.

39:40.628 --> 39:42.213
[chuckles]

39:43.214 --> 39:45.758
[playful music]

39:46.759 --> 39:51.347
I can see that you've worked very hard
on these drawings.

39:51.430 --> 39:53.766
[sighs]
It's good for nothing.

39:53.849 --> 39:56.894
I don't even know
where I should go with all of it.

39:59.313 --> 40:01.107
Why did you choose the penguin?

40:02.400 --> 40:03.484
They're cute. Why not?

40:03.567 --> 40:05.403
In what way are they cute?

40:05.486 --> 40:06.987
Hmm…

40:07.071 --> 40:11.534
Well, I think about the way they walk,
it's adorable.

40:12.326 --> 40:16.622
Waddle, waddle.
[chuckles]

40:16.705 --> 40:17.832
[groans]

40:18.791 --> 40:23.754
They, um, don't walk
that way to look cute.

40:24.463 --> 40:25.464
Sorry?

40:26.424 --> 40:31.595
Um, penguins waddle
'cause their ambulation is…

40:31.679 --> 40:34.515
They follow a pendulum system.

40:34.598 --> 40:38.269
If a pendulum reaches
its peak on one side,

40:38.352 --> 40:42.648
it pauses for a moment for the energy
to change from potential back to kinetic.

40:44.108 --> 40:46.569
Uh… Yeah.

40:46.652 --> 40:47.945
Oh…

40:48.571 --> 40:51.657
I had no idea. Okay. So?

40:52.199 --> 40:53.033
Uh…

40:53.701 --> 40:54.785
So?

40:55.661 --> 40:57.371
- Uh…
- [pages rustle]

40:58.789 --> 41:01.375
- When the penguin waddles like that…
- Uh-huh.

41:01.459 --> 41:04.753
…it can save up to 80 percent
of the energy it needs.

41:04.837 --> 41:06.130
Mm, save energy.

41:07.798 --> 41:13.345
So, uh, the really cool thing
about them is this real efficiency.

41:13.429 --> 41:16.765
- Oh, really? Hmm.
- [chuckles]

41:16.849 --> 41:20.352
[mumbling]
Eighty percent…

41:20.436 --> 41:22.480
[Seok-ho giggles]

41:23.355 --> 41:24.773
Uh, also…

41:25.524 --> 41:28.694
the penguins' blood vessels
are wrapped in a very unique pattern.

41:28.777 --> 41:29.987
The "wonder net."

41:30.070 --> 41:33.032
The veins and arteries
are all intertwined, so…

41:33.115 --> 41:35.951
Whoa, you really know a lot.

41:36.535 --> 41:39.205
[giggles]
You are a zoologist!

41:39.288 --> 41:40.331
[Seok-ho] No, no.

41:46.879 --> 41:48.380
Everyone's taking their time, huh?

41:48.464 --> 41:51.008
Yeah, they all said
they would run a little late.

41:51.717 --> 41:56.639
Maybe we should order something first?
Here, Director. We're all hungry.

41:56.722 --> 42:00.935
- Oh, no. You, Ms. Oh.
- Ah, um, what should we order?

42:01.018 --> 42:03.312
[Soo-jin] Let's start
with some pork belly. Yeah.

42:03.395 --> 42:05.523
[Myung-ju] Hmm, that okay, Director?

42:09.276 --> 42:12.780
[gentle music]

42:16.784 --> 42:18.619
- [bell chimes]
- [sighs]

42:19.495 --> 42:20.329
Ooh.

42:27.878 --> 42:31.090
Go ahead. You young people
love this kind of thing.

42:31.173 --> 42:32.508
Oh, okay.

42:32.591 --> 42:35.594
Uh, why did you want
to meet all of a sudden?

42:35.678 --> 42:38.138
[sighs]
Let's eat first, and then we'll talk.

42:38.222 --> 42:39.682
- Uh…
- [utensils clanking]

42:40.307 --> 42:41.517
Ooh.

42:44.311 --> 42:45.187
[Mrs. Bae giggles]

42:48.482 --> 42:49.483
[Mrs. Bae] Uh…

42:50.484 --> 42:52.695
How's Ha-kyung doing now?

42:54.113 --> 42:58.117
She's swamped with work
because of the heat wave.

42:59.285 --> 43:02.663
She hasn't said anything
since my last visit with her, though?

43:02.746 --> 43:05.207
No. Not really. No.

43:07.501 --> 43:09.211
I was so off guard.

43:10.671 --> 43:12.965
She threw the not-getting-married thing
at me,

43:13.048 --> 43:17.595
and I was mortified, I had to back off,
and let it all just go.

43:18.554 --> 43:22.099
Ah, you know, the one who lives upstairs--

43:22.182 --> 43:24.560
Not Seok-ho, not that man.

43:24.643 --> 43:25.686
Why?

43:25.769 --> 43:27.229
He's not right for the Director.

43:27.313 --> 43:30.190
Their personalities, tastes,
hobbies, lifestyles,

43:30.274 --> 43:32.109
nothing in common at all.

43:32.776 --> 43:34.361
I can say that for sure.

43:34.445 --> 43:37.406
Ah, but they can find those things
when they're together.

43:38.073 --> 43:40.409
To put it bluntly,
they're two different people,

43:40.492 --> 43:42.286
two different lives, two sets of parents.

43:42.369 --> 43:45.497
I mean, how can everything
be perfect from the beginning?

43:46.332 --> 43:48.709
It would be weird
if there were no differences.

43:50.919 --> 43:53.088
You… have a point.

43:53.172 --> 43:58.260
You see, marriage isn't about
a couple perfectly coming together.

43:58.844 --> 44:03.390
The joining comes first,
so they can perfect each other, huh?

44:04.308 --> 44:09.730
This process is what married life is for,
so at the end of that is a good couple.

44:11.023 --> 44:15.235
Young people these days think
that it's some kind of insurance plan

44:15.319 --> 44:17.821
or just some sort of big legal headache.

44:17.905 --> 44:19.782
That's why most won't even give it a try.

44:19.865 --> 44:24.078
They're busy calculating
all the conditions and the concerns.

44:24.828 --> 44:27.581
You've never regretted yours, then?

44:28.374 --> 44:29.375
What?

44:29.458 --> 44:31.502
Your own marriage, you know?

44:33.128 --> 44:34.421
[breathes deeply]

44:34.505 --> 44:35.798
Well, uh…

44:35.881 --> 44:37.716
I've always regretted it.

44:37.800 --> 44:41.387
I've said that he's my worst enemy
and I hope lightning kills him.

44:42.054 --> 44:43.097
But…

44:43.639 --> 44:46.433
if someone asks me if I would do it again,

44:47.226 --> 44:51.355
if I could somehow go back in time,
well, I'd probably say yes.

44:52.147 --> 44:53.357
Why?

44:53.440 --> 44:55.109
[chuckles]

44:55.192 --> 44:58.237
Through it all, we had
some pretty good times, him and I, too.

44:58.320 --> 45:00.656
Especially with Tae-kyung and Ha-kyung.

45:00.739 --> 45:05.869
And those girls are the finest works
I've ever created.

45:05.953 --> 45:07.621
[chuckles]

45:10.040 --> 45:14.753
- So what I want to say to you is--
- But still, I really mean it.

45:14.837 --> 45:17.256
Not Seok-ho. Not with Ha-kyung.

45:18.048 --> 45:19.299
Not ever.

45:19.967 --> 45:21.844
Why are you being so obstinate?

45:21.927 --> 45:23.095
Who are you to say?

45:24.638 --> 45:27.558
[light music]

45:27.641 --> 45:29.685
Oh, the pizza is getting cold, ma'am.

45:29.768 --> 45:32.604
[awkward chuckle]
Please. I'll grab you a slice.

45:44.324 --> 45:45.451
Mm.

46:01.967 --> 46:03.093
[sighs]

46:05.137 --> 46:07.306
Looks like our dinner's not working out.

46:07.389 --> 46:08.223
What do you mean?

46:08.307 --> 46:11.226
[Myung-ju] We're having it right now.
Quite deliciously, I might add.

46:12.019 --> 46:15.689
Mrs. Oh, looks like you forgot
why you called for this event.

46:15.772 --> 46:17.733
First, it's to say goodbye
to Forecaster Lee.

46:17.816 --> 46:20.694
Second, it's supposed to be
the first ever get-together

46:20.777 --> 46:22.488
of our current team, isn't it?

46:23.572 --> 46:25.407
Well, what can we do now?

46:25.908 --> 46:27.784
They're not gonna show up.

46:28.827 --> 46:30.662
It's their loss if they're not here.

46:31.163 --> 46:33.457
Even though the Director herself
put it together.

46:33.540 --> 46:35.042
[Myung-ju] We can't control them.

46:36.710 --> 46:38.295
Everything is what it is.

46:38.879 --> 46:40.756
So let's get two more orders.

46:41.423 --> 46:43.008
We'll rename this night

46:43.091 --> 46:46.720
as a well-deserved retreat
just for the women of Team Two.

46:46.803 --> 46:48.722
Do you approve, Director?

46:48.805 --> 46:50.057
What do you say?

46:50.891 --> 46:51.808
Okay.

46:51.892 --> 46:54.853
- A women's retreat sounds great.
- [giggles]

46:54.937 --> 46:57.272
Sir, could we please get
two more pork belly orders?

46:57.356 --> 46:59.483
- Soju too.
- [man] You got it.

46:59.566 --> 47:00.651
We're ordering some soju?

47:00.734 --> 47:03.237
Well, now that we've re-christened
our night, we might as well.

47:03.320 --> 47:05.030
- Ooh!
- How's that sound?

47:05.656 --> 47:07.115
Mm, thanks.

47:09.368 --> 47:10.661
[tapping]

47:11.245 --> 47:13.247
Oh, wow. Oh, wow. Oh, wow.

47:13.330 --> 47:15.082
[chuckling]

47:16.750 --> 47:19.044
- Here you go.
- Oh, yes. All right.

47:22.422 --> 47:24.258
- Noraebang later?
- Well, of course!

47:24.341 --> 47:25.759
- Of course.
- Yay!

47:25.842 --> 47:26.927
- Cheers.
- [Soo-jin] Cheers.

47:27.010 --> 47:27.928
[Myung-ju] Cheers.

47:28.011 --> 47:31.640
- [Myung-ju] Let's go. Let's go.
- [Soo-jin] Let's go. This place!

47:31.723 --> 47:34.184
[laughter]

47:34.268 --> 47:36.603
Do we have to go in here?
I have to go home.

47:36.687 --> 47:39.106
- Hey! Why are you going home?
- Let's barbecue now!

47:39.189 --> 47:41.775
- You are such a good singer.
- Come on. Just one more.

47:41.858 --> 47:44.403
- [laughter]
- I'm a high soprano.

47:44.486 --> 47:47.781
- High soprano.
- I don't think their songs in low keys

47:47.864 --> 47:49.324
are real songs.

47:50.450 --> 47:52.286
- [Myung-ju] I'm a baritone.
- [all laughing]

47:52.369 --> 47:53.495
[laughter]

47:53.579 --> 47:55.789
[line ringing]

48:04.298 --> 48:06.341
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

48:06.425 --> 48:07.301
[beeps]

48:10.887 --> 48:11.847
[sighs]

48:15.142 --> 48:16.685
[gentle music]

48:24.901 --> 48:27.195
[phone vibrates]

48:28.572 --> 48:29.781
Yes, Ms. Oh.

48:32.534 --> 48:33.744
Where are you right now?

48:38.123 --> 48:41.043
[Myung-ju] The Director is so drunk.

48:41.126 --> 48:43.128
I have to go home now.

48:43.211 --> 48:46.506
I'm sorry but can you come
pick her up, Forecaster Lee?

48:48.342 --> 48:49.301
[sighs]

48:53.930 --> 48:55.182
[Si-woo] I'm here.

48:59.478 --> 49:00.771
How drunk are you?

49:03.106 --> 49:04.358
Can you walk on your own?

49:15.452 --> 49:17.663
I want things to work out.

49:19.748 --> 49:23.085
I want things to work out
for the two of us.

49:28.548 --> 49:29.675
But…

49:31.760 --> 49:33.345
that's the only thing.

49:35.889 --> 49:41.395
A love that stays under control
with tempered feelings.

49:41.478 --> 49:43.689
I like it simple and stable.

49:45.440 --> 49:48.193
If things start to go beyond moderate…

49:50.487 --> 49:52.322
I become anxious.

49:55.826 --> 49:57.285
Then I feel…

49:58.328 --> 50:01.373
I become someone else and not myself.

50:03.375 --> 50:05.919
[gentle music]

50:06.002 --> 50:07.504
So all I can do…

50:09.423 --> 50:11.216
is do it moderately.

50:14.886 --> 50:16.513
Get up. Let's take you back home.

50:17.973 --> 50:19.933
So then you should decide.

50:21.476 --> 50:23.895
You should decide while you're in Jeju.

50:29.568 --> 50:33.655
If you think you can do it
moderately or not.

50:34.156 --> 50:36.616
Really think about it then decide.

50:42.164 --> 50:44.750
[Si-woo] One of my superiors once told me…

50:46.251 --> 50:48.295
that when I don't understand
a satellite image,

50:48.378 --> 50:50.714
no matter how long I've looked at it,

50:50.797 --> 50:56.762
I should stand a little further away
and observe the flow of the clouds."

50:57.262 --> 50:59.890
[emotional music]

51:19.868 --> 51:23.830
To be honest, I didn't understand
what he said at the time.

51:23.914 --> 51:27.626
I've never seen a satellite image
I didn't understand back then,

51:27.709 --> 51:30.921
and I was very confident
about everything related to weather.

51:36.259 --> 51:37.302
Then…

51:38.386 --> 51:39.513
I met you.

51:40.847 --> 51:42.390
[emotional music fades]

51:52.025 --> 51:53.276
[gasps]

52:11.002 --> 52:12.963
Oh, my head.
[groans]

52:16.633 --> 52:19.427
[breathes deeply]

52:21.263 --> 52:23.431
[Ha-kyung] Oh.
[chuckles]

52:28.228 --> 52:30.105
[groans]

52:35.485 --> 52:36.570
[door opens]

52:38.989 --> 52:40.365
[door closes]

52:40.991 --> 52:43.910
Oh, you're flying right after work?

52:45.495 --> 52:46.538
That's my stuff.

52:46.621 --> 52:47.706
Oh, you scared me.

52:49.708 --> 52:50.876
[sighs]

52:50.959 --> 52:53.879
- [door closes]
- Uh, are you moving home?

52:53.962 --> 52:56.089
No. I was thinking I would stay
at the office again

52:56.172 --> 52:58.008
since it's typhoon season, you know.

52:59.384 --> 53:00.468
Where is Lee Si-woo?

53:01.052 --> 53:02.262
Si-woo left.

53:02.345 --> 53:03.471
Sorry?

53:03.555 --> 53:07.225
Jeju. He left today. You didn't know?

53:09.394 --> 53:12.898
Anyway, soup over there
to nurse your head.

53:16.192 --> 53:18.695
[wistful music]

53:21.489 --> 53:25.410
[plane zooming]

53:29.247 --> 53:31.249
[wistful music]

53:38.965 --> 53:40.175
[Si-woo] Did you know

53:40.842 --> 53:44.387
you were the strangest weather
I've ever seen in my life?

53:45.889 --> 53:46.890
[sighs]

53:56.650 --> 53:58.443
Uh…
[gasps]

53:59.444 --> 54:00.612
There was an accident? Where?

54:00.695 --> 54:02.072
Where and how bad is it?

54:02.155 --> 54:03.156
[Ha-kyung] I…

54:03.865 --> 54:05.158
Hold on a moment. Who is this?

54:05.241 --> 54:06.868
If you tell me
which hospital it is, I'll--

54:06.952 --> 54:08.286
[Yu-jin] This is Chae Yu-jin.

54:13.750 --> 54:14.709
[sighs]

54:15.418 --> 54:17.128
I'm with Si-woo right now.

54:18.713 --> 54:20.340
[winces]

54:20.423 --> 54:22.425
[pensive music]

54:34.187 --> 54:36.022
[phone vibrates]

54:41.236 --> 54:43.989
- [sighs]
- [phone vibrates]

54:45.615 --> 54:46.533
Hello?

54:47.742 --> 54:49.202
Why are you calling me so late?

54:51.746 --> 54:53.123
Wait, what's that?

54:53.915 --> 54:56.501
[Ki-jun panting]

54:56.584 --> 54:59.379
Ha-kyung. What the hell's going on?

54:59.963 --> 55:01.423
Lee Si-woo is hurt.

55:01.506 --> 55:02.716
Okay, I get Lee Si-woo is hurt.

55:02.799 --> 55:05.135
But why on earth
is he there right now with Yu-jin?

55:05.719 --> 55:07.470
- Coincidence.
- What?

55:08.596 --> 55:10.557
In Jeju, they ran into each other.

55:12.267 --> 55:13.393
[sighs]

55:14.728 --> 55:16.604
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

55:21.901 --> 55:24.237
[tense music]

55:35.790 --> 55:37.167
Lee Si-woo.

55:39.335 --> 55:40.754
[sighs]

55:44.299 --> 55:46.009
This is all your fault.

55:46.593 --> 55:47.927
How is this my fault?

55:48.011 --> 55:51.056
I was so scared
of an office romance because of you,

55:51.139 --> 55:54.142
that I was always on edge
with Si-woo and so afraid.

55:54.726 --> 55:59.272
Uh, you were always on edge
and scared even when you were with me.

55:59.355 --> 56:01.775
I was scared of you!
[sobs]

56:02.609 --> 56:07.489
I was so consumed
by the fear of getting hurt.

56:07.572 --> 56:11.367
Now that I never told him
how I really felt.

56:11.451 --> 56:13.328
Or did anything.

56:17.123 --> 56:19.042
Now what do I do?

56:19.626 --> 56:21.127
What do I do?

56:21.211 --> 56:22.378
[Ha-kyung sobbing]

56:22.462 --> 56:25.006
What do I do now?

56:25.090 --> 56:26.966
[Ha-kyung bawling]

56:34.557 --> 56:37.477
[Ha-kyung] So it wasn't because
of Lee Si-woo's principle

56:37.560 --> 56:39.646
of not wanting to get married.

56:40.563 --> 56:43.274
I was scared that it would get too hot,

56:43.358 --> 56:45.819
too hot to the point
where I can't control it.

56:46.402 --> 56:51.491
I was afraid to lose control
of my emotions, so I was making excuses

56:52.784 --> 56:57.080
to stop the last one degree from rising
to reach the boiling point.

56:58.081 --> 56:59.165
But…

57:00.458 --> 57:01.918
[Dong-han sighs]

57:06.047 --> 57:08.174
- Mr. Um.
- [Dong-han] Hmm?

57:08.258 --> 57:11.302
[foreboding music]

57:13.138 --> 57:16.808
- Wow. When did that start, huh?
- Oh!

57:23.398 --> 57:25.233
[phone ringing]

57:27.026 --> 57:29.279
Hello. Headquarters. This is Um.

57:30.363 --> 57:31.656
Yeah. We just saw it.

57:32.157 --> 57:33.283
It is a…

57:33.783 --> 57:34.701
[Sung] Typhoon, yes.

57:34.784 --> 57:37.620
Number 15 Elisha
that was following Number 14 Ricky.

57:38.371 --> 57:41.249
Around eleven o'clock today,
it was moving northeastward,

57:41.332 --> 57:43.084
300km near Okinawa.

57:43.168 --> 57:46.254
The central pressure was 990,
max wind velocity 20 per second,

57:46.337 --> 57:47.964
and a radius of 150.

57:48.047 --> 57:49.466
- [man] That's it.
- Can I have that?

57:49.549 --> 57:50.425
[indistinct chatter]

57:50.508 --> 57:52.135
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

57:52.218 --> 57:54.888
[man] Satellite Center. Can you check
the intensity of the typhoon?

57:54.971 --> 57:59.559
At 10:00 p.m., we're looking at a path
straight for the southern Jeju Sea,

57:59.642 --> 58:03.188
120km over the western sea near Okinawa.

58:03.271 --> 58:06.691
980 central pressure,
max velocity, 28, strong wind, 200.

58:06.774 --> 58:08.693
[Dong-han sighs]

58:08.776 --> 58:11.237
Mm, I understand.

58:11.321 --> 58:14.782
- Keep sending us the data. Mm-hmm.
- [phone clanks]

58:15.366 --> 58:16.242
- Mr. Shin.
- [Seok-ho] Yes?

58:16.326 --> 58:18.203
Give me data on ocean heat change
by time period.

58:18.286 --> 58:19.329
- Yes, sir.
- [Dong-han] Ms. Oh.

58:19.412 --> 58:20.705
Figure out steering current flow

58:20.788 --> 58:22.832
and the vertical wind sheer
from the updated forecast.

58:22.916 --> 58:24.167
[Myung-ju] Yes, sir.

58:24.250 --> 58:25.335
VERTICAL WIND SHEAR:
CHANGE IN WINDSPEED WITH HEIGHT

58:25.418 --> 58:26.794
STEERING FLOW: THE FLOW
THAT INFLUENCES TYPHOON MOVEMENT

58:26.878 --> 58:29.964
[unsettling music]

58:33.885 --> 58:36.804
[tense music]

58:43.978 --> 58:45.104
[door handle clanks]

58:55.949 --> 58:59.327
You're all dead, all of you.

59:00.787 --> 59:03.498
[unsettling music]

59:29.983 --> 59:31.651
[Ha-kyung sobbing]

59:35.780 --> 59:38.449
[sobbing continues]

59:44.247 --> 59:49.377
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

59:49.460 --> 59:51.462
[suspenseful music]

59:58.219 --> 59:59.262
[thunder roars]

01:00:02.974 --> 01:00:04.976
["Open Your Heart" by Lyn playing]

01:00:27.165 --> 01:00:29.417
[Ki-jun] I didn't realize
you were so invested.

01:00:29.959 --> 01:00:33.755
Who knows what I feel?
It seems like everything's falling apart.

01:00:33.838 --> 01:00:35.256
I want to talk to the guy in charge.

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:37.050
- I can't calm down!
- What's going on?

01:00:37.133 --> 01:00:38.926
[Ki-jun] What you're doing
is obstructing official duties.

01:00:39.010 --> 01:00:40.887
It's important
that they can do their work.

01:00:41.679 --> 01:00:45.933
[Hyang-rae] No. No more. Just be
a decent man for once and sign it.

01:00:46.517 --> 01:00:48.770
[Ki-jun] Except Yu-jin left me now, so…

01:00:48.853 --> 01:00:50.229
Can you let me go?

01:00:50.313 --> 01:00:52.982
Is there any way
I could come along to Jeju Island?

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:56.611
[Ha-kyung] There's so much that we expect
people we love to figure out.

01:00:56.694 --> 01:00:59.864
But what if we took nothing for granted

01:00:59.947 --> 01:01:01.741
- and said everything explicitly?
- Yu-jin.

01:01:01.824 --> 01:01:04.911
[Si-woo] All I really wanted was time
to realign and be together.

01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:07.580
I must have missed where we fell out.
